<http://data.silknow.org/object/c683e743-e40a-3df1-9873-7d7753f75ab2>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Panels from a woman's petticoat, 1740-1760, British; Chinese blue silk satin, quilted with sunflowers and diamond pattern"@en , "Two and a quarter panels of a woman’s petticoat of blue silk satin, lined with linen striped in white and two shades of red, and wadded with a layer of dark blue wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with blue silk thread in a horizontal pattern of an undulating leafy vine with sunflowers against a background of parallel diagonal lines at the hem, with a 1 inch (2.5 cm) by ¾ inch (1.9 cm) diamond pattern above.  The hem has been cut off."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/d68d7a1a-25d9-309f-9d4d-91066b3727bf> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/c9d9f2fe-e99a-3ae8-9743-61016427c29d> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/06d2bf6b-74e2-3274-90bf-1bbabb63d5c2> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Two and a quarter panels of a woman’s petticoat of blue silk satin, lined with linen striped in white and two shades of red, and wadded with a layer of dark blue wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with blue silk thread in a horizontal pattern of an undulating leafy vine with sunflowers against a background of parallel diagonal lines at the hem, with a 1 inch (2.5 cm) by ¾ inch (1.9 cm) diamond pattern above.  The hem has been cut off."@en , "Panels from a woman's petticoat, 1740-1760, British; Chinese blue silk satin, quilted with sunflowers and diamond pattern"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/c683e743-e40a-3df1-9873-7d7753f75ab2/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/c683e743-e40a-3df1-9873-7d7753f75ab2/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/c683e743-e40a-3df1-9873-7d7753f75ab2/dimension/3> ;
